# The cache-sweep module's own texts: its name and the line under it.
brain-task-cache-sweep = Sweep the caches
brain-task-cache-sweep-does = Deletes the folders in your cache that nothing has used for a while, judged by the last time each one was used. A cache can always be made again, so what you lose is the time to remake it, never your work. It never follows a link out of the cache, never crosses into another file system, and keeps anything dated in the future.
brain-task-cache-sweep-brief = Deletes the cache folders that nothing has used for a while.
